# end-station builder emissions (regenerate: python3 sw/builder/endstation_builder.py <cfg>)
sw/builder/out/

# Per-config builder outputs. ONLY <cfg>/gen/ is tracked - those are the .svh
# headers the RTL `include-s. The flat files beside it (build_plan.md,
# aem_overlay.json, soc_params.json, ...) are build products of
# whichever config last ran and belong to nobody. They were swept into the tree
# twice on 2026-08-11 by a `git add configs/generated`, once carrying 5,194
# lines and a build_plan.md that then broke the docs gate with 12 bare-reference
# findings. The negation must name the DIRECTORY: git will not descend into an
# excluded directory, so `!.../gen/**` alone would never match.
configs/generated/*/*
!configs/generated/*/gen/

