# run_all_suites.sh output. The GLOB matters: every campaign picks its own
# suffix (--outdir .suite-logs-<tag>), so a bare `.suite-logs/` let 57 log
# files into the tree under `.suite-logs-final/` (added incidentally by
# 8a1d7d1d) where a later sweep silently MODIFIED tracked files.
.suite-logs*/
*.launch.log
# scripts/run_all_suites.sh whole-sweep lock: concurrent sweeps share the
# per-suite obj_* build dirs, so the second one refuses rather than corrupt it
/.run_all_suites.lock
/.run_all_suites.lock.owner

tb/verilator/*/obj_*/
wedge.vcd

# Session handovers are working notes: local paths, bench host names and
# live board detail belong in them, and none of that belongs in a public
# repo. The older tracked ones predate this rule and stay for their history.
#
# A GLOB, not a filename (2026-08-11). This rule named `HANDOVER_0808.md`
# literally, so it protected exactly one file and the NEXT handover would have
# been untracked-but-not-ignored - one `git add -A` from publication. Measured
# at the time: HANDOVER_0808 carries 19 hits of the gate's own deny patterns
# (bench hosts, /home paths, the retired evidence token) and HANDOVER_0804
# carries 5, while every handover that reached origin/main carries zero. The
# separation was working by luck of one hand-maintained line; now it is a rule.
HANDOVER_*.md
handover_*.md

# generated at build time by the protocol-processor ROM/microcode builders
configs/generated/*.hex
syn/yosys/*.hex

# syn/yosys/ooc_selftest.py builds mutated copies of ooc.sh beside it (the
# script derives the repository root from its own location, so they cannot
# live elsewhere), and ooc.sh --record-rom-digests stages the ledger rewrite
# in place. Both are swept on exit and on SIGINT/SIGTERM; these lines cover
# the SIGKILL and CI-timeout cases, so a stray copy of the gate script is
# never one broad `git add` from a commit (#191/#192).
syn/yosys/.ooc-mut-*
syn/yosys/.ooc-pkg-*
syn/yosys/rom_digests.tsv.new.*

# syn/ooc/ooc_tcl_selftest.py writes its mutated recipes beside ITSELF for
# the same reason (milan_datapath_ooc.tcl derives $REPO from [info script],
# so a mutant must live in syn/ooc/). Its package mutants take no dir= and
# land in $TMPDIR, so they need no entry.
syn/ooc/.ooc-mut-*

# local agent scratch, never shipped
.claude/

# Vivado xvlog leaves these in its working dir; scripts/xvlog_gate.py runs it
# in a tempdir, but a raw `xvlog` invocation from the tree would drop them here.
xvlog.pb
xvlog.log
xsim.dir/
.Xil/
